  "worked_solution": "First, notice that there are $16$ cups in $1$ gallon. So, to find the unit price per cup, we divide the total price by $16:$\n\n$$\n36÷16=2.25\n$$\n\nTherefore, purchasing the lemonade costs $$2.25$ per cup.",
